## `Split`

``` hol4
markerLib.Split : thm -> thm
markerLib.destSplit : thm -> thm
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Marks a theorem as a split rule for the extension simplifier.

`Split th` proves `marker$Split p` from `th : A |- p`, keeping the
hypotheses. `destSplit` undoes this. `markerLib.dest_directive` reports
`Split th` as `DSplit th`.

The marker is honoured only by the extension simplifier, where it adds `th`
as a split rule for one call (see `simpExtLib.Split`). The ordinary
simplifier fails if given it.

### Failure

Never fails. `destSplit` returns a theorem without `marker$Split`
constants unchanged.

### Example

``` hol4
>> markerLib.Split (ASSUME “p:bool”);
>> markerLib.destSplit it;
```

### See also

[`simpExtLib.Split`](#simpExtLib.Split),
[`markerLib.ExclX`](#markerLib.ExclX),
[`markerLib.strip_wrappers`](#markerLib.strip_wrappers).
